  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-discord",
      "text": "[](https://dshmarketplace.dev/plugins?q=dsh-discord)\n\nBidirectional Discord bridge and remote controller for DeepSeek Harness.\n\nListed in the independent community-run [DSH Marketplace](https://dshmarketplace.dev/plugins?q=dsh-discord) ([source](https://github.com/DshMarketPlace/dshmarketplace))."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-discord",
      "text": "The dedicated `discord` profile supports one owner and project across DMs, guild text channels, and threads. Each Discord conversation owns an independently persisted DSH Session. Owner DMs trigger directly; ordinary guild-channel messages require an explicit bot mention; an already-bound thread continues without repeated mentions. Slash commands never require a mention."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-discord",
      "text": "The bot invite requests View Channel, Send Messages, **Send Messages in Threads**, Read Message History, Embed Links, and Attach Files. `doctor` checks the same permission set. Discord server and channel permissions determine where the bot is visible; the plugin remains single-owner and fail-closed."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-discord",
      "text": "The controller includes natural text, `/dsh help/status/new/stop/steer`, coalesced progress, approvals, structured questions, image and text/code attachment ingress, durable event deduplication, Gateway reconnect, and managed daemon operation.\n\nEnable **Message Content Intent** on the Discord Developer Portal Bot page for natural guild-channel messages.\n\n```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "Until an npm release is available, install the CLI from GitHub.",
      "text": "npm install --global github:suuuuuu-1/dsh-discord\ndsh-discord setup --package-spec github:suuuuuu-1/dsh-discord\ndsh-discord doctor\ndsh-discord start"
    },
    {
      "section": "or managed background mode",
      "text": "dsh-discord start --daemon\ndsh-discord status\ndsh-discord stop\n```\n\nThe global CLI is only a launcher. The plugin itself is activated in the dedicated `discord` profile and remains bound to the single project selected during setup; it does not become active in every directory or in the `web` profile.\n\nThe Bot Token is stored only through DSH Credentials. See [README.zh.md](README.zh.md), [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md), and [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md)."
    }
  ],
